  "id": "PAPER-paper-method-043",
  "track": "paper",
  "title": "NeuroPictor: Refining fMRI-to-Image Reconstruction via Multi-individual Pretraining and Multi-level Modulation",
  "status": "source_unresolved",
  "objective": "surpass_source_paper_same_task",
  "goal": "Surpass the source-paper result on the same task: Generate the natural image viewed by a subject from that subject's fMRI; preserve both semantic and structural reconstruction assessment. Retrieval-only, caption prediction or encoder reconstruction is not the same output.",
  "primary_outputs": [
    "Candidate method and outputs for the source task: Generate the natural image viewed by a subject from that subject's fMRI; preserve both semantic and structural reconstruction assessment. Retrieval-only, caption prediction or encoder reconstruction is not the same output.",
    "Source-paper comparison for Proposed Inception-v3 two-way identification, with all eight Table 1 metrics retained and panel guardrails unresolved: Retain all eight Table 1 metrics: mean pixel Pearson r; source SSIM; AlexNet features.4/features.11, Inception avgpool and CLIP image-feature two-way identification; EfficientNet and SwAV correlation distances. For N images, identification is mean_j [sum_(i != j) 1(corr(real_i,pred_j)<corr(real_j,pred_j))/(N-1)], with ties failing. Higher is better except the two distances. Identification arithmetic is verified from the pinned code, but native parity for the complete panel is unresolved because the historical SSIM environment and grayscale multichannel semantics are not fixed."
  ],
  "success_criteria": [
    "Recover and freeze the original complete train/test image and session membership, all four evaluation subjects and all eight pretraining-subject inputs.",
    "Reproduce the final fine-tuned NeuroPictor reference with source metric parity and authenticated image/feature identity; keep the published score distinct from the rerun.",
    "Before candidate freeze, resolve the proposed primary choice, meaningful effect, full-panel guardrails, uncertainty and matched budgets.",
    "Exceed the source-paper baseline and matched author rerun under that fixed same-task rule. No subject-1 subset, new image split, easier prior access, best-of-many generation or prospective SSIM substitution can establish the paper win.",
    "The bound improvement contract must be improvement_ready and its complete same-task comparison and admission requirements must pass.",
    "Reproduction is calibration only; reconstructing a numerical result, changing the task or split, or achieving stronger significance alone is not success."
  ],
